{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/911935-covers-when-not-in-use","id":911935,"title":"Covers when not in use?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-10T15:44:47-07:00","id":911935,"title":"Covers when not in use?","content":"Apologies in advance if this is a stupid question, but what happens to any additional Covers a Demon may have while they're wearing one of them? I know they're in a sort of quantum Schrodinger's &quot;they exist but they don't state,&quot; but does everyone at the office notice that Terry hasn't come in for a few weeks? Conversely, would not checking in on your stored Covers risk compromise?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:41:17-07:00","id":911966,"title":"","content":"I had the same questions when I read Demon, basiclly when you're not your cover that person doesn't exist on auto pilot without you. If your cover has a job and you don't work it the cover might loose the job, or will if you miss several days of work in a row","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:41:58-07:00","id":911967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/911935-covers-when-not-in-use#post911935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies in advance if this is a stupid question, but what happens to any additional Covers a Demon may have while they're wearing one of them? I know they're in a sort of quantum Schrodinger's &quot;they exist but they don't state,&quot; but does everyone at the office notice that Terry hasn't come in for a few weeks? Conversely, would not checking in on your stored Covers risk compromise?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not living your other Covers' lives enough causes them to degrade, yeah. I don't recall the page number, but things like unexplained disappearances lead to Compromise rolls. Part of the danger of multiple Covers is having to juggle all those lives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T16:44:50-07:00","id":911970,"title":"","content":"Remember, compromise checks for <i>grossly</i> out of character behavior. It's not <i>grossly</i> out of character to go missing for a few days here or there; everybody has unexpected things come up, stuff they get busy with. But if not a single soul sees or hears Terry for two months because he's off being somebody else, to the point where people would get concerned for his health or safety, that's unusual for most people. You don't want to juggle more Covers at once than you can keep in the air, with the general exception of burn Covers that have few relationships to check up on and pose little danger if they degrade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T05:13:58-07:00","id":912193,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this very thing is one of the issues I'm wrestling with for Institutional Covers. Best thing I can think of is going for a group that <i>can</i> disappear for a time, focusing solely on the Institution, or setting up an Alibi Gadget to run it on autopilot while you deal with other stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T12:22:22-07:00","id":912374,"title":"","content":"Also, the Covers that are not in use age as normal. If you use a single Cover for years, and then put on another, people will who recognize it will notice the aging, and probably ask where in the world you've been. Compromise rolls for lack of use will probably destroy them before old age, though. As a side note, while unused Covers age, other biological processes are frozen. They won't starve, suffer from atrophied muscles or any of that.<br /> <br /> If a Demon doesn't think he can juggle multiple Covers, he can acquire Facades, which are simplistic Covers with an effective rating of 1. Facades do not take up your Cover slots, so he can have as many as he wants. However, they cannot be used to Go Loud, and their minimal rating makes them very fragile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T16:13:38-07:00","id":912505,"title":"","content":"Your cover is held in quantum storage. They are no-where till you become that cover.While they are in storage they continue to age but luckly you know exactly when your cover will die naturally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-12T06:54:12-07:00","id":912774,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar522_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"522\" data-vbnamecard=\"522\">Stupid Loserman</a> Also highlights the importance of taking Covers that won't be suspicious. The reason you help the single mother get on her feet and independent of her parents is so that when the time comes, you can step into her life and not have people asking where she is. When you patchwork a Cover, you definitely don't want them to be On Call at the hospital.<br /> <br /> Although I will say one of the things I couldn't wrap my head around in regards to Patchwork Covers is how they get their shit. You make Deals for relationships, not actual changes. I remember the book saying that if you take someone's relationship with their girlfriend, only the girlfriend's memory changes. Her parents wonder who you are, and where the girl she was dating went. All the photos stay the same. So how does a Cover end up getting a house, or even an appearance? I don't really remember the corebook going into detail on that, even though it mentions how Low Cover might be represented by all your clothes looking the same and your apartment not fitting into the building's layout. That seems more like how things would work for an Angel or your original Cover, but once you've made deals and crafted, stolen, or bartered for a life, that house is real and after a while you're probably buying your own clothes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}